Start a setuid-root server with an environment of its own.

The libraries the server loads while it is still root read the environment
for debugging and tuning, and the C library's set-id protection covers only the
loader's own variables: Mesa, loaded by glamor before the server drops root,
opens the file GALLIUM_TRACE names for writing -- as root, so
`GALLIUM_TRACE=/etc/shadow startx' truncated any file on the system.  The
server needs nothing from the caller's environment; for an elevated start it
is cleared before anything runs and PATH is set to the system's.  A server
started by root is unchanged.

